+# Repo Mirrors Health Design
+
+## Goal
+
+Add a repo-level Mirrors tab that shows which ForkMesh nodes mirror the current repository and whether each mirror is healthy enough to browse or clone.
+The first implementation slice is API-backed and table-first.
+The network graph, durable uptime history, region, and relay metadata are follow-up work.
+
+## Current State
+
+The public website already has a repository detail page with tabs for Code, Commits, Issues, Pull requests, Discussions, and a placeholder Network tab.
+The catalog client already groups logical mirrors by `rootCommit`, falling back to the repo name when no root commit is published.
+The Worker already stores public repository catalog records in D1.
+Those records include `owner`, `name`, `hostedSince`, `lastSync`, `sizeBytes`, `rootCommit`, `visibility`, and `source`.
+The Worker also stores `host_presence` for currently live repository host tunnels and `repo_first_hosted` for the first time a repository was seen live.
+
+## Desired User Experience
+
+On a repository page, the existing Network tab becomes a Mirrors tab.
+Opening the Mirrors tab shows summary metrics and a table.
+The required table columns are Node, Status, Last seen, Hosted since, Sync age, and Clone available.
+The page must make ForkMesh's distributed nature visible without making the user understand implementation internals.
+The page must not claim a clone will pass integrity verification before Git actually receives the advertised refs from the host.
+
+## Scope
+
+The first slice includes a Worker endpoint for mirror health, the repo page Mirrors tab, summary metrics, loading and empty states, responsive layout, and automated tests.
+The first slice does not include a graphical network map.
+The first slice does not include long-term uptime percentages because current `host_presence` rows are live presence rows, not durable history.
+The first slice does not include region or relay labels because no reliable region or relay field is currently published by the catalog.
+
+## Worker API
+
+Add `GET /api/repo/{owner}/{repo}/mirrors`.
+The route returns only public repository mirrors.
+Private repository mirror health can be added later with the existing view-token model.
+The route resolves the requested repo from the catalog.
+It then finds every public catalog row with the same logical mirror key.
+The logical mirror key is `rootCommit` when present and the lowercased repository name otherwise.
+The route joins live presence from `host_presence` and first-hosted timestamps from `repo_first_hosted`.
+
+The response shape is:
+
+```json
+{
+  "ok": true,
+  "owner": "mainnode",
+  "repo": "forkmesh",
+  "groupKey": "root:abc123",
+  "generatedAt": 1782300000000,
+  "summary": {
+    "mirrors": 3,
+    "online": 2,
+    "cloneAvailable": 2,
+    "dataHostedBytes": 192308123,
+    "longestHostedSince": 1778700000000,
+    "freshestSync": 1782299940000
+  },
+  "mirrors": [
+    {
+      "node": "mainnode",
+      "owner": "mainnode",
+      "repo": "forkmesh",
+      "status": "online",
+      "lastSeen": 1782299990000,
+      "hostedSince": 1778700000000,
+      "syncAgeMs": 60000,
+      "lastSync": 1782299940000,
+      "behind": false,
+      "cloneAvailable": true,
+      "sizeBytes": 64000000,
+      "source": "local-node"
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+If the requested repository is not published or is private, the endpoint returns `404`.
+If a catalog row has malformed numeric fields, the endpoint treats that field as absent rather than failing the whole response.
+Mirrors sort by online status first, then freshest `lastSync`, then node name.
+
+## Frontend
+
+Rename the repo detail tab label from Network to Mirrors.
+Keep the existing tab style and icon language.
+Load mirror health lazily when the Mirrors tab is opened.
+Render four summary metrics above the table: Mirror nodes, Clone availability, Longest hosted, and Data hosted.
+Render a table with the requested columns.
+Use existing status-pill styling for Online, Offline, and Behind states.
+Show `not recent` when the Worker has no current `lastSeen` value for an offline mirror.
+Show `Yes` for clone availability only when a live host is present for that mirror.
+Show `No` for offline public mirrors.
+Use relative time in the cells and keep absolute timestamps available through `title` attributes.
+On small screens, the table must collapse into readable row blocks without horizontal overflow.
+
+## Data Interpretation
+
+Status is Online when `host_presence.ts` is within `HOST_PRESENCE_STALE_MS`.
+Status is Offline otherwise.
+Last seen is `host_presence.ts` when the row exists and is live enough to be useful.
+Hosted since is the catalog `hostedSince` value, falling back to `repo_first_hosted.ts`.
+Sync age is `generatedAt - lastSync`.
+A mirror is behind when its `lastSync` is more than the existing five second tolerance behind the freshest mirror in the group.
+Behind is a sync warning, not a replacement for online or offline status.
+Clone availability is true when the mirror has a live host.
+
+## Testing
+
+Worker tests must cover grouping mirrors by `rootCommit`.
+Worker tests must cover fallback grouping by repository name.
+Worker tests must cover online status, last seen, hosted since fallback, sync age, clone availability, and sorting.
+Worker tests must cover private or unpublished repositories not being returned.
+Frontend tests can be lightweight source-contract tests because the public site is plain static HTML and JavaScript.
+Browser verification must inspect desktop and mobile layouts after implementation.
+
+## Risks
+
+Current live presence does not preserve a durable last-seen history after stale rows are pruned.
+The UI should therefore describe stale mirrors as `not recent`, not as a precise offline timestamp.
+Clone availability is a reachability signal, not an integrity guarantee.
+The Git smart HTTP path still performs the authoritative state-hash check during clone.
+
+## Future Work
+
+Add a graph view after the table contract is stable.
+Add durable per-node uptime samples if the product needs uptime percentages.
+Add region and relay fields once desktop nodes or federated relays publish trustworthy metadata.
+Add authenticated private repo mirror health after the public mirrors flow is complete.
